I haven't been there enough times to find it extremely boring yet, but
I can understand why some do.

I think the most interesting part of the game is the beginning, where
you build your character, gain new levels and skills fast, get better
equipment all the time, identify new and exciting items, etc.

Once you have maxed all stats and found all the very best equipment,
which you usually do before you enter Gehennom, the rest of the game
is mostly "routine". You just have to get through it to win, only
stupid mistakes can kill you, and your character or equipment will not
get better.

Maybe it would be more interesting if the best weapons, spells and
other equipment were only available after you had reached Gehennom?

